commit b30800c5a57a39ef379444de579a9f0117682821
Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 03:36:55 2026 +0200

    probe: promote 20 screened benchmarks into auto, keep bbq screening
    
    The probe (auto_probe, --final-only at 600M/1B/1.7B) answered its question:
    INCLUDE v2 clears the gate in 42 of 42 languages at 1.7B, and every lettered
    candidate is rescued by its rf_ twin (mmlu 0.001 -> 0.057, commonsense_qa
    0.002 -> 0.188, bbh_mcq 0/17 -> 10/17 tasks, acp_bench_mcq 0/7 -> 5/7). All
    twenty join groups.auto, so every checkpoint is topped up with them and they
    enter every RQ -- a population change, stated in RULES.md. bbq stays a
    candidate: it clears a 1/12 chance at 0.44 without saying much, and costs
    23 min per checkpoint against 2.9 for mmlu and 0.3 for a belebele task.
    
    The tooling that decides it, reusing what exists:
    - probe.sh chains derive -> ladder report -> gate -> compare -> survivors.
    - probe_survivors.py reads the committed mask alone and writes the gate per
      language, original vs rf_ twin.
    - compare.py gains --families/--tag and subtracts each task's own chance
      level instead of a hardcoded 0.25, so 2- to 10-way pairs read on the scale
      the 4-way families already used; proven to leave those families' numbers
      identical (max |delta margin| 0.00 over 40 cells).
    - ladder_report._trained_tasks reads SNR_TRAINED_GROUPS (default auto), the
      opt-in that let the probe be gated before promotion.
    
    Three fixes found by running it:
    - derive_task_options opened all 4.0M sample files on every pass; with
      --only-missing it is 75 s instead of an hour, and it filled n_items for 227
      tasks -- all 288 probe tasks now match an independent harness count exactly.
    - truthfulqa_mc2 is _APPROX: its score is probability mass over all true
      answers, so the derived 1/4 would have been a chance level every model
      clears.
    - bbq is 36 task-minutes in submit_eval's walltime weight; without it a solo
      top-up got 15 minutes, the kill is not a recorded failure, and the watcher
      resubmitted it forever.
    
    Also: INCLUDE v2 moved into auto_probe (one group, not two: 85 jobs and
    48.5 node-h against 161 and 86), the rfgm_belebele registration and its 59
    YAMLs (rewrite finished 52,944 of 53,100 rows), and evals/CLAUDE.md no longer
    claims a running watcher re-reads tasks.json -- it does not, which is why a
    promotion only takes effect when the watcher is restarted.

